  "body": "## APG-2664 — Decommission NEC pipeline in prod namespace (PR 1 of 3)\r\n\r\nNamespace: `hmpps-manage-and-deliver-accredited-programmes-prod` ONLY.\r\n\r\n### Background\r\n\r\nNEC has decommissioned the nightly SQL Server .bak transfer. The final file (`backup-production-IM-dbo-only-20260909013009.bak`) landed at 01:30 UTC on Wed 9 Sep 2026 and successfully ingested to both preprod and prod RDS at 05:45 / 06:30 UTC on Thu 10 Sep 2026. Both RDS instances have been manually snapshotted before this PR — snapshot IDs, ARNs and KMS key ARNs are recorded in the APG-2664 Jira ticket.\r\n\r\n### What this PR does\r\n\r\n**Kubernetes manifests**\r\n- `cronjob-s3-transfer.yaml` — `spec.suspend: true` + warning banner\r\n- `db_restore.yaml` — `spec.suspend: true` + warning banner + both `SQLSERVER_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET_NAME` env vars invalidated to `APG-2664-DECOMMISSIONED` (belt-and-braces: any accidental unsuspend fails at S3 lookup before the destructive DB restore)\r\n- `db_restore_one_off.yaml` — deleted (git history preserves it)\r\n\r\n**Terraform**\r\n- `resources/rds-sqlserver.tf` — `deletion_protection = true` on `module.sqlserver`\r\n- `resources/s3.tf`:\r\n  - Removed 14-day `expire-old-backups` lifecycle rule from `sqlserver_backup_s3_bucket` (bucket is currently empty and won't receive new writes)\r\n  - New `module.archive_s3_bucket`: versioning on, no lifecycle, bucket policy denies `s3:DeleteObject*`, `s3:DeleteObjectVersion*`, `s3:DeleteBucket`, `s3:DeleteBucketPolicy` for `Principal: \"*\"`\r\n  - New `kubernetes_secret.archive_s3_bucket` with `lifecycle.prevent_destroy = true` as a Terraform tripwire\r\n- `resources/irsa.tf` — added `archive_s3_bucket_policy` to `irsa-sqlserver.role_policy_arns` so the existing `sqlserver-service-pod` can PUT the final `.bak` into archive (delete still blocked by bucket policy)\r\n\r\n### Deliberately NOT touched here\r\n\r\n- Legacy `s3_bucket` module + `im-backup-s3` secret (deferred to PR 3 after app-team confirms no consumer)\r\n- `preprod_backup_s3_read` cross-namespace IAM (needed for the post-merge archive copy)\r\n- `upload_s3_bucket_policy` — NEC's IAM role is only granted in preprod's version, so **PR 2 (preprod) is the PR that technically revokes NEC's DataSync access.**\r\n\r\n### Post-merge runbook (executed manually, not committed)\r\n\r\n1. Copy `backup-production-IM-dbo-only-20260909013009.bak` from the preprod backup bucket into the new prod archive bucket via `sqlserver-service-pod`\r\n2. Verify deny-delete: `aws s3 rm` from the same pod must return AccessDenied\r\n3. Record destination VersionId + size + ETag in APG-2664 Jira\r\n4. `kubectl delete job db-restore-from-preprod-001` — clean up stale Failed Job instance from a previous manual apply\r\n5. \r\n---\r\nTicket: APG-2664\r\nBranch: `APG-2664/prod-disable-nec-pipeline`\r\nPR sequence: this = 1 of 3 (prod freeze) → PR 2 (preprod cut + NEC IAM revoke) → PR 3 (cleanup)\r\n",
